Z||000000||Greg Piet||03-04-2001||05:47 PM||||Earlier this year someone mentioned a 2.8 to 3.1 stroker kit from <A HREF="http://www.engine-parts.com/Online_catalog/onlinestore.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.engine-parts.com/Online_catalog/onlinestore.html</A> <BR>called a PRO-BUILDER® GM 2.8-3.1 STROKER ENGINE KIT.<P>I have sent an inquiry to the company as to its compatability with our 60 degree v6's (namely a 1985 motor with the external harmonic balancer), but I am curious if anyone else had dealt with this company, or knows reasons why this kit would be bad or good.  I know there are some very knowledgeable folks here in this area, and since you own a Fiero as well I hold great weight in your words of wisdom.<P>I have never undertaken any performance boring/stroking kit rebuilds as all my previous engine rebuilds have been ressurections back to stock specs or as close to stock as possible.  Since my experience in this area is zero I am rather concerned that I will overlook something important. <P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72<BR>#47 CSP<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.physics.unlv.edu/~gregpiet/Jan1617s.jpg">  <BR>Our lady of blessed acceleration dont fail me now!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||03-04-2001||08:47 PM||||I don't know what they include in that kit, but all you need to stroke the 2.8 to 3.1 is the 3.1 crank.  That's the only difference between the 2.8 and 3.1 (disregarding the FWD models).  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||bubbajoexx||03-04-2001||08:58 PM||||not just the crank you need the pistons as well the differance in stroke raises the wrist pin height in the piston to maintane the proper deck height ps leave the pilons alone||||reg||1
Z||000003||Greg Piet||03-04-2001||09:07 PM||||What about the difference between internal and external harmonic balancers? 85 v6 vs 88 v6<P>I swear the pylon jumped under my car!  It was suicide  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula 18||03-04-2001||10:39 PM||||I am not sure about harmonic balancer but I do know that the 88 and later aer internaly balanced and need a new flywheel. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Greg Piet||06-12-2001||07:30 PM||||OK my Stroker from ARI is DONE!!!!<BR>I LOVE IT!<BR>3.1 stroker kit with 040 over pistons<BR>double roller timing chain<BR>ARI Balanced my flywheel, and it uses the stock harmonic balancer.<BR>Stage 2 Camshaft<BR>Fiero Store Performance heads<BR>1.52 roller rockers<BR>ported stock exh manifolds<BR>power pulley<BR>Block decked and bored by local machine shop<BR>ARI is a nice group of folks and were very quick and helpful.<P>Everything worked well<BR>OODLES of power from 3000-5700+ RPM.<P>I reccomend that kit to anyone!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dave Gunsul||06-12-2001||07:57 PM||||When building a 3.1 you need: the crank, pistons, and flywheel/flexplate because the<BR>3.1 crank is internally balanced.<BR>It's also a good idea to get either an adj. fuel regulator or the lucas type injectors to<BR>help tweak the engine.<BR>Most of the places that sell 3.1 stroker kits include most, if not all, of these parts. You can use a flywheel/flexplate from an 88 Fiero. GM still sells the 88 flywheel/flexplate and the flexplate is a beefier unit than the original.<BR>All Fiero V6 harmonic balancers are at zero balance and will work with either a external or internally balanced engine, just make sure<BR>it's still in good shape.<P>Pisa also sells a stroker kit.<BR>Pisa'a web-site: <A HREF="http://www.cybercars.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cybercars.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000007||voyagerspe||06-12-2001||11:25 PM||||I did the 3.4 storker from ARI.  Great company to deal with, you should have no problems with them.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000008||Formula88||06-12-2001||11:41 PM||||How'd that 3.4 stroker kit work for you?  It sounds like the better deal instead of the 3.4 F-body engine.  Especially if you already have the 2.8.||||reg||5
Z||000009||voyagerspe||06-13-2001||12:18 AM||||I love the engine. but its not a kit you have to buy the 3.4 from them.  however the price is resenable 900 doller range for the short block.  goto there web site for the specs.  This motor blows away 2.8's . ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Greg Piet||06-13-2001||03:54 AM||||If I remnember correctly, the 3.4 ARI is THIN WALLED!<BR>So they have not done testing on thier 3.4 with a blower.<P>I think the ARI guy I talked to (ALAN?) said they give no guarantee if you put in a blower, but I thought a 3.1 blown would be a lot safer than their 3.4 and I think they actually put assisted aspiration in one of thier 3.1 rebuilds (I reccomend asking them personally as my memory is bad).<BR>Regardless I figure 7-9 psi would be safe and I thought one would be at about 250+ hp.<P>The 3.4 may be amazing, but with the 3.1      the first time out at an autocross I beat a 350 formula firebird with a 20 yr driver on race rubber (I have race rubber too).  <P>I also toasted a 76-78 camaro on a stop light derby (THEY STARTED IT, and I wanted to test my new motor anyhows...  I know I know they didnt hold a gun to my head)||||reg||1
Z||000011||Raydar||06-13-2001||10:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Greg Piet:<BR><B>If I remnember correctly, the 3.4 ARI is THIN WALLED!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It <I>is</I> thin walled. <BR>They bore out "selected" 2.8 blocks. Apparently, some of the blocks are too thin when they're bored that far, due to casting variations. <BR>They have to sonic test them. <P>Makes me wonder what percentage of 2.8s are useable for this, and how reliable they'll be. <BR>Of course if they warranty them, they can't be too fragile.<P>BTW... NOS voids the warranty their 3.1. Not sure about turbos or S/C.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
Z||000012||Formula88||06-13-2001||12:42 PM||||Then maybe that F-body 3.4 [b]is[\b] the better deal afterall.  I don't want something stretched to the limit of durability.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Greg Piet||06-13-2001||08:29 PM||||That may be a wise move Formula.<BR>I was gonna do their 3.4 but when I realized how far they pushed the envelope on their motor, I decided to just go with the 3.1 which required much less "other" mods.||||reg||1
